# One rule per line: label<TAB>regex. Matching ignores case. Read by guard.ps1 and guard.sh.
skips or focuses a test	\b(it|test|describe|context)\.(skip|only|todo)\(|(?<![\w.])(xit|xtest|xdescribe|fdescribe)\(|@pytest\.mark\.(skip|xfail)|pytest\.skip\(|@unittest\.skip|@(Disabled|Ignore)\b|#\[ignore\]|\bt\.Skip(f|Now)?\(|\[\s*(Fact|Theory|InlineData|MemberData|ClassData)\s*\([^\]\n]*\bSkip\s*=|\bSkip\.If(Not)?\(|\[\s*(Test|TestMethod|TestCase|Fact|Theory)\b[^\]\n]*,\s*(Ignore|Explicit)\b|\[\s*(Ignore|Explicit)\s*\(\s*"|\[\s*(Ignore|Explicit)\s*\]\s*\n\s*(\[|public|internal|private|async|void)\b|\bAssert\.(Skip|Ignore|Inconclusive)\(
has an empty catch	catch\s*(\([^)]*\))?\s*\{\s*\}
has a bare except	\bexcept\s*:
swallows an exception with pass	\bexcept\b[^\n:]*:\s*(pass|\.\.\.)\s*(\n|$)
swallows a promise rejection	\.catch\(\s*\(?\s*\w*\s*\)?\s*=>\s*(\{\s*\}|null|undefined)\s*\)
returns a fallback from a catch	catch\s*(\([^)]*\))?\s*\{\s*return\s*(null|undefined|\[\]|\{\}|false|''|"")?\s*;?\s*\}
